<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 22 January, from 1517 to 1973.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1517 <span class="tih-ago">509 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ottomans defeat the Mamluks at Ridaniya outside Cairo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Selim I's army, with superior artillery and firearms, crushed the Mamluk forces just outside Cairo. The victory ended the Mamluk Sultanate and brought Egypt, Syria and the Hejaz under Ottoman rule.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/selim-i">Selim I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1760 <span class="tih-ago">266 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British defeat the French at Wandiwash</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sir Eyre Coote's East India Company army beat the Comte de Lally's French force in the Carnatic. The battle effectively ended French hopes of empire in India.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1879 <span class="tih-ago">147 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Zulu army destroys a British force at Isandlwana</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 20,000 Zulu warriors overran a British camp at Isandlwana, killing over 1,300 soldiers and African auxiliaries. It was one of the worst defeats of the British army in the colonial era.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1901 <span class="tih-ago">125 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Queen Victoria dies at Osborne House</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Victoria died on the Isle of Wight aged 81 after reigning for 63 years, then the longest reign in British history. Her son succeeded as Edward VII.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1905 <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bloody Sunday in St Petersburg sparks revolution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Imperial troops fired on unarmed workers led by Father Georgy Gapon marching to petition Tsar Nicholas II, killing many. The massacre set off the 1905 Revolution and badly damaged faith in the Tsar.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1944 <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allied troops land at Anzio</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Operation Shingle, Allied forces landed behind German lines south of Rome, hoping to outflank the Gustav Line. Quickly contained, they endured four months of hard fighting before breaking out.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1973 <span class="tih-ago">53 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Supreme Court decides Roe v. Wade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">By seven votes to two, the Court ruled that the constitutional right to privacy protected a woman's decision to have an abortion. The ruling was overturned in 2022.</p></div></li></ol>
